{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2475 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "244cef4ea47e88eb95bb74ffd2ec82bcd2950f6fad055539a7d8f8f984ea17e3" :edb/db-before-t 2474 :edb/db-after-t 2475 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535787 50 #inst "2026-10-09T07:12:06.156Z" 13194139535787 true] [17592186078358 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366279 13194139535787 true] [17592186078359 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366258 13194139535787 true] [17592186078359 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366265 13194139535787 true] [17592186078360 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366272 13194139535787 true] [17592186078874 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535787 true] [17592186078874 1100 "Find $F^{′}(0)$ if $F(x) = ∫_{x}^{\\sin (x)}\\sqrt[3]{1 + t^{2}}dt$." 13194139535787 false] [17592186078874 1100 "Find ${F}^{′}(0)$ if $F(x)={\\int }_{x}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.$" 13194139535787 true] [17592186078874 1145 "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{x}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{x}^{a}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $x$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nThe integrand $\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt[3]{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{du}}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt[3]{1+{x}^{2}}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\sqrt[3]{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\sqrt[3]{1+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))^{2}}-\\sqrt[3]{1+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\sqrt[3]{1+{sin}^{2}⁡(x)}-\\sqrt[3]{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${F}^{′}(0).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(0) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)\\sqrt[3]{1+{sin}^{2}⁡(0)}-\\sqrt[3]{1+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\sqrt[3]{1}-\\sqrt[3]{1} \\\\  & =1-1 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366258 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366259 13194139535787 true] [17592186366258 1089 "q-116501" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366258 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535787 true] [17592186366258 1100 "For $x>0,$ find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366258 1113 #uuid "a3359bd2-48fb-59d6-ba98-93f115a49404" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366258 1145 "To compute ${f}^{′}(x),$ we first make the substitution $u={x}^{2}$ and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{0}^{u}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integrand is continuous on $[0,u],$ and so by FTC II we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot u\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{u} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})\\cdot u\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{u} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366260 13194139535787 true] [17592186366259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366261 13194139535787 true] [17592186366259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366262 13194139535787 true] [17592186366259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366263 13194139535787 true] [17592186366259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366264 13194139535787 true] [17592186366259 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535787 true] [17592186366259 1041 "selection" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366259 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366264 13194139535787 true] [17592186366259 1110 #uuid "9f8850dd-662c-5c77-822a-e1e3e6aa5880" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366260 1034 "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{x}" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366260 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366260 1111 #uuid "da048bd9-dc9a-50c0-af83-2b20072066fc" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366261 1034 "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{x}" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366261 1111 #uuid "220cddc0-c466-5dbb-b6e3-43bc099f566f" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366262 1034 "\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366262 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366262 1111 #uuid "60e3e31e-30e9-54b5-9172-49580f7ed8cf" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366263 1034 "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366263 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366263 1111 #uuid "feb24f6d-16b3-581e-804d-ef18536ea554" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366264 1034 "2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366264 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366264 1111 #uuid "b31d9cec-e44d-5e1d-8ef2-481068b09d08" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366265 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366266 13194139535787 true] [17592186366265 1089 "q-116504" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366265 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535787 true] [17592186366265 1100 "Determine ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{3x-5}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t.$" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366265 1113 #uuid "f496b800-2ee8-5e43-a695-4b3e8a838990" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366265 1145 "To compute ${f}^{′}(x),$ we first make the substitution $u=3x-5$ and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{3x-5}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{u}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit $u$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of the definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{u}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(-{\\int }_{1}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{1}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{1}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2u-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-5)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2u-1)) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(3x-5)-1) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x-11).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366267 13194139535787 true] [17592186366266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366268 13194139535787 true] [17592186366266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366269 13194139535787 true] [17592186366266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366270 13194139535787 true] [17592186366266 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366271 13194139535787 true] [17592186366266 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535787 true] [17592186366266 1041 "selection" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366266 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366270 13194139535787 true] [17592186366266 1110 #uuid "a6d8105d-5f9f-5b10-b6c1-79aa5aa0078e" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366267 1034 "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-1)" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366267 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366267 1111 #uuid "28c9f74a-2f55-5aa7-950e-aa47da69c492" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366268 1034 "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366268 1111 #uuid "4942eb32-f8ea-584f-8871-735413e1a855" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366269 1034 "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-11)" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366269 1111 #uuid "ba1a8f2d-807f-543c-b853-55b7e69b3536" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366270 1034 "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x-11)" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366270 1111 #uuid "5faf8e07-f4e3-5e39-abcf-3ccb6f01231e" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366271 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x-11)" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366271 1111 #uuid "736bc42e-57b3-5f50-8aba-6d19a3773b84" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366272 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366273 13194139535787 true] [17592186366272 1089 "q-116548" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366272 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535787 true] [17592186366272 1100 "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{x}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t.$" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366272 1113 #uuid "70a0aba7-0b5b-5702-ba2e-1ffda4c05a18" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366272 1145 "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{x}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{x}^{a}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{x}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $x$ and ${3}^{x}+2.$\n\nThe integrand $(6t-7)$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying the FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{x}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-(6x-7)+\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =7-6x+({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))(6u-7) \\\\  & =7-6x+({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))(6({3}^{x}+2)-7) \\\\  & =7-6x+({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))(6\\cdot {3}^{x}+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u={3}^{x}+2.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${f}^{′}(0).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =7-6(0)+({3}^{0}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))(6\\cdot {3}^{0}+5) \\\\  & =7+11\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366273 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366274 13194139535787 true] [17592186366273 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366275 13194139535787 true] [17592186366273 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366276 13194139535787 true] [17592186366273 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366277 13194139535787 true] [17592186366273 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366278 13194139535787 true] [17592186366273 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535787 true] [17592186366273 1041 "selection" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366273 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366277 13194139535787 true] [17592186366273 1110 #uuid "24240ad9-c85e-50b8-9a3d-62011c712b64" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366274 1034 "7\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366274 1111 #uuid "b4d687a7-5b56-51cc-a2e5-1e5dd3769983" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366275 1034 "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-5" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366275 1111 #uuid "f0a7aaef-775e-5c38-a90c-3b27c798a832" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366276 1034 "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+5" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366276 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366276 1111 #uuid "fa8daae6-c46c-59c0-b4bc-632d83530bd9" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366277 1034 "11\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+7" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366277 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366277 1111 #uuid "67fa7e2e-b529-5b31-b2c0-733c60bd4f3d" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366278 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-1" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366278 1111 #uuid "30a894d7-4c60-578d-8a3c-b50a5ab08cbd" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366279 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366280 13194139535787 true] [17592186366279 1089 "q-75221" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366279 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535787 true] [17592186366279 1100 "Let $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)-x.$ Find ${g}^{′}(2)$ given the function is defined by $g(x)={\\int }_{x}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.$" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366279 1113 #uuid "71788e1c-b47b-5cdc-ab12-b5675e14b728" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366279 1145 "In this example, the variable limit $x$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\ng(x)={\\int }_{x}^{0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t=-{\\int }_{0}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{x}^{0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{0}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{0}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of ${g}^{′}(2),$ we substitute $x=2$ in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(2) & =-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 2)-2) \\\\  & =-(0-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366280 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366281 13194139535787 true] [17592186366280 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366282 13194139535787 true] [17592186366280 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366283 13194139535787 true] [17592186366280 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366284 13194139535787 true] [17592186366280 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366285 13194139535787 true] [17592186366280 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535787 true] [17592186366280 1041 "selection" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366280 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366281 13194139535787 true] [17592186366280 1110 #uuid "2e7ccd6d-95ff-5bdd-bd86-a85c5563fa5f" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366281 1034 "{g}^{′}(2)=2" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366281 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366281 1111 #uuid "42c6c102-1213-5b92-a66e-a68563ddf4f9" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366282 1034 "{g}^{′}(2)=1" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366282 1111 #uuid "cb0c9c36-1945-558d-a753-2ab62d123bf3" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366283 1034 "{g}^{′}(2)=-1" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366283 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366283 1111 #uuid "ff134327-c31d-5c37-89f5-2c0bce6c3642" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366284 1034 "{g}^{′}(2)=-2" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366284 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787 true] [17592186366284 1111 #uuid "9cdebea1-63d9-550e-92b5-6e047eefe076" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366285 1034 "{g}^{′}(2)=0" 13194139535787 true] [17592186366285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535787